"Meisters are powerful but inflexible, with almost no leeway in choosing skills."
"Examples include Sword Meister and Trap Meister."
"A C-rank Meister may still do well in the right specialty."
"Meister is the weaponmaster class; single-weapon subtypes offer few choices."
"An S- or A-rank Meister's first skill usually keeps them from being disarmed."
"The second skill picks an offensive style; the third raises a class stat."
"Meister spells buff one's own weapon, and those buffs are boring below S-rank."
"Close-combat Meisters are almost purely geared toward offense."
"Swordmaster is a common Meister subtype."
"A Meister needs their tool; subtypes include Staves, Bow, Spear, Knives and the Mind Writher."
"A Meister of Bow can recall arrows; a Meister of Torches can weld with magic."
"Tool-breaking skills like Flickerer do not work on Meister tools."
"Most Meisters will not let others touch their tools."
